#5300
Outside the Western Gates of Mytherandil~
   You leave the city of Mytherandil behind and walk down a well-trodden
path toward what appears to be an arena of some sort.  Even from here
you can see many battles under way, each fenced off from the rest, and
the screams of spectators carry on the wind.  The western gates of the
city lie to the east, and the road continues west.
~
53 c 0
D1
~
~
0 0 1173
D3
~
~
0 0 5301
S
#5301
Road to the Arena~
   As you draw closer to the arena, you see that it is far bigger than
you first thought.  A great wall divides the battlefield in two, and on
the far side rise wooden stands packed with screaming spectators.
Pennants flutter above them, and the dust of the fighting hangs over
everything like a haze.  The road leads east toward the city and west to
Arena Road.
~
53 c 0
D1
~
~
0 0 5300
D3
~
~
0 0 5302
S
#5302
Southeast Corner of Arena Road~
   You stand on the cobblestone path known as Arena Road at a corner of
the battlefield.  From here you can see two entrances to the arena: to
the south, a large gate through which the fighters come and go, and to
the east, a ramp leading up onto the great wall that divides the
battlefield, where archers keep watch to make sure there is no foul
play.  Crowds of excited fans throng the corner.  The road continues
north and west around the arena, a dirt road leads south away from it,
and the road to Mytherandil lies east.
~
