#5379
A Wooden Alcove~
   The road grows narrow and finally fades away as you enter a small
wooden alcove.  The trees bend inward overhead as if to shelter this
place from the sun, and soft, green grass grows thick beneath them,
dotted with tiny white flowers.  The air here is clear and fresh
compared to that of the lands around it, and a deep calm settles over
you.  The way out lies west.
~
