S
#5471
The Ring~
   A round pit of raked white sand, sunk below the level of the battlefield
and walled in by smooth stone twice the height of a man, so that nothing
that goes in comes out without leave.  Iron gates on either side lead to
the pens.  Above the wall the stands climb away on every side, and the
noise of the crowd beats down like heat.  Dark stains in the sand are
raked over between bouts, and never quite go away.
~
53 cgj 0
S
#5472
The Fighters' Pens~
   A row of stone stalls behind iron bars, where the Arena's fighters wait
their turn in the ring.  It smells of sweat, straw and old blood.  A
trainer's whip hangs on a hook by the gate.
~
